      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mry77qf403lhftsb",
          "message": {
            "text": "`text` and `markdown` are no longer the same string.\n\nSARIF §3.11.9 requires `text` whenever `markdown` is present, and its NOTE gives the reason: the message must stay viewable where formatting isn't rendered. §3.11.3 adds that a plain text message \"SHALL NOT contain formatting information\". Writing the markdown source into both fields satisfied the letter and defeated the purpose — a third-party SARIF viewer showed literal `###` and `**`.\n\n`flattenMarkdown` (in `src/utils/flattenMarkdown.ts`) produces the fallback. It keeps list, blockquote, and thematic-break markers, which read as intended unrendered, and drops only what is noise in plain text.\n\n**Ordering mattered:** this had to land *after* the reader started preferring `message.markdown` (see the note on `noteBody` in `src/review-notes/store.ts`). Shipped in the other order, Glassbox's own reader — which took `text` — would have started displaying the flattened version of every note.\n\nVerified end-to-end by writing a note with the working-tree CLI and reading the shard back: `markdown` byte-identical to the input, `text` flattened.",
            "markdown": "`text` and `markdown` are no longer the same string.\n\nSARIF §3.11.9 requires `text` whenever `markdown` is present, and its NOTE gives the reason: the message must stay viewable where formatting isn't rendered. §3.11.3 adds that a plain text message \"SHALL NOT contain formatting information\". Writing the markdown source into both fields satisfied the letter and defeated the purpose — a third-party SARIF viewer showed literal `###` and `**`.\n\n`flattenMarkdown` (in `src/utils/flattenMarkdown.ts`) produces the fallback. It keeps list, blockquote, and thematic-break markers, which read as intended unrendered, and drops only what is noise in plain text.\n\n**Ordering mattered:** this had to land *after* the reader started preferring `message.markdown` (see the note on `noteBody` in `src/review-notes/store.ts`). Shipped in the other order, Glassbox's own reader — which took `text` — would have started displaying the flattened version of every note.\n\nVerified end-to-end by writing a note with the working-tree CLI and reading the shard back: `markdown` byte-identical to the input, `text` flattened."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/review-notes/sarif.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 88,
                  "endLine": 99,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " * so both write sites stay in step.\n */\nexport function noteMessage(body: string): { text: string; markdown: string } {\n  const flat = flattenMarkdown(body);\n  // `text` must be non-empty when present; fall back to the source in the\n  // pathological case where flattening leaves nothing.\n  return { text: flat === '' ? body : flat, markdown: body };\n}\n\n/**\n * Map a note to a SARIF `result`. Standard fields carry everything except\n * `confidence`, which has no SARIF home and goes in the namespaced"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
